{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"spinal-grayish-perch","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Report\n\n`scripts/canary_bridge.py:31` does a bare `import alert_dedup`. That only resolves when `scripts/` is already on `sys.path`. Running the affected test file on its own fails:\n\n```\n$ python -m pytest tests/unit/test_reconcile_bridge_canary_class.py -q\nERROR ...::test_every_bug_close_carries_valid_class[heartbeat-alert-_heartbeat_recovery_env]\n  - ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'alert_dedup'\nERROR ...::test_every_bug_close_carries_valid_class[binding-drift-alert-_drift_recovery_env]\n  - ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'alert_dedup'\n1 passed, 2 errors\n```\n\nReproduced on `origin/main` with the repo venv on PATH.\n\n## Provenance — introduced today, not pre-existing\n\n`scripts/alert_dedup.py` was ADDED by `0767c38ebb` (ticket 63e8, 'route dependency advisories by lane'). That change correctly EXTRACTED the dedup helpers out of `canary_bridge.py` rather than duplicating them — the extraction was the right call — but it left the consumer importing the new module by bare name.\n\nAn agent working an unrelated ticket hit this and reported it as 'pre-existing … unrelated', which is true of their change but not of the tree: it is hours old.\n\n## Why it matters even though CI is green\n\nCI's full run passes, because something upstream puts `scripts/` on `sys.path` before the module is imported. The failure only appears when the file is run as a SUBSET — which is what developers and agents do constantly while iterating. A test that passes in CI and fails when you run it directly trains people to distrust the suite.\n\n## This is a known class in this repo, with a fix landed TODAY\n\nTicket `a371` (merged `1db88c92d7`) was the same shape: `tests/unit/test_audit_ticket_page.py` used a `tests.`-rooted import that could not resolve under bare `pytest`, masked because it sat below an `importorskip`. Its fix added a standing guard, `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py`, which AST-scans for `tests.`-rooted imports anywhere under `tests/`.\n\nThat guard does NOT cover this case: it looks for `tests.`-rooted imports inside `tests/`, not for bare imports of `scripts/` modules. So the class is only half-guarded.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_reconcile_bridge_canary_class.py` passes standalone, with the repo venv on PATH and no wrapper\n- [ ] The import is resolved by an explicit, invocation-independent mechanism — not by relying on ambient `sys.path` ordering. Decide and state which: a package-relative import, an explicit path insert at a documented seam, or making `scripts/` a real package\n- [ ] The remaining sibling call sites are swept — `canary_bridge.py` is unlikely to be the only bare cross-module import under `scripts/`; enumerate them and state which are safe and why\n- [ ] The `a371` guard is EXTENDED (or a companion added) so a bare import of a `scripts/` module that only resolves under one invocation style fails a test, closing the other half of the class\n- [ ] A test proves the guard is RED against the current defect before the fix\n\n## Note for whoever takes it\n\nThis is the SECOND regression to reach main from `0767c38ebb` within hours; the first was a stale `--force-close` call site in `scripts/dependency_audit.py` (fixed under 24f7, guard added in `839477cd72`). Both slipped because the change was authored concurrently with others and validated against a tree that no longer matched main. The recorded lesson from that one applies here: a sweep is only valid as of the sha it ran against — re-run it against merged main before pushing.","id":"291e-7b48-3f24-41c6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"canary_bridge's bare 'import alert_dedup' resolves only when scripts/ is on sys.path; subset test runs error"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786122868627208001,"uuid":"62302265-6941-4fbe-9371-4330f1726943"}